 "id": "capset",
 "title": "Cap set problem",
 "statement": {
  "text": "In affine geometry, a cap set is a subset of the affine space  where no three elements sum to the zero vector.\nThe cap set problem is the problem of finding the size of the largest possible cap set, as a function of . The first few cap set sizes are 1, 2, 4, 9, 20, 45, 112, ....",
  "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cap_set"
